\subparagraph{Organization.}
%As in~\cite{DBLP:journals/corr/abs-2402-08346},
We use the \LD\ problem to demonstrate key technical concepts, and explain how to adopt the arguments for \TCPB. 
%regarding lower bounds and algorithms.
%The arguments regarding \TCPB\ follows almost the identical
%line.
We use the standard notations that are mentioned in 
Section~\ref{sec:prelims}.
Theorem~\ref{thm:LD-struct-vc} is proved in Section~\ref{sec:vc-fpt}. 
In the same section, we
show how to modify the techniques to obtain similar results
for other parameters like twin-cover number and 
distance to clique, and we observe that \LD 
admits a linear kernel when parameterized by neighbourhood diversity.
The proof of Theorem~\ref{thm:LD-struct-fes}
is given in Section~\ref{sec:fes-kernel} whereas
Theorem~\ref{thm:loc-dom-set-incompressibility}
is proved in Section~\ref{sec:incompressibility}.
We conclude the paper with some open problems in 
Section~\ref{sec:conclusion}.

