\item Florent believes that there is a simple argument that implies a kernel 
with $\calO(2^{d} \cdot k)$ vertices where $k$ is a solution size and $d$ is a twin-width 
of the input graph.
This implies $\binom{\calO(2^{d} \cdot k)}{k} = 2^{\calO(d k + k \log(k))}$ algorithm.
However, \textsc{Dominating Set} admits $2^{\calO(d^2 \cdot k)}$ algorithm.
I am very interested to try and get algorithm of the form $2^{\calO(d^2 \cdot k)}$ (or better)
for \textsc{Locating-dominating Set}.

\item Check https://arxiv.org/pdf/2309.15645.pdf to see 
