+"""Verified Test Cover generator for arXiv:2411.17948.
+
+The paper's incompressibility proof gives an explicit reduction from Red-Blue
+Dominating Set to Test Cover.  This module applies that exact gadget to the
+edge-set cover of a regular bipartite graph.  A cover of size q in the source
+is a perfect matching.  One matching is planted as y = 2*x+b (mod q), so its
+certificate is known before the Test Cover instance is assembled.
+
+The answer is a compact but concrete encoding of the selected tests: entry x
+is the right endpoint y of source-edge test X_(x,y), and all forced gadget
+tests Z_h are included by definition.  Verification expands the selected
+tests' exact incidence signatures and checks that every pair of items is
+distinguished.  It never reads inst["answer"].
+"""
