codex
I’ve fixed the construction: the solver gets a genuine finite Test Cover instance, represented exactly by parity tests on all binary items. A planted full-rank cyclic orbit is chosen first; decoy tests have identical one-test statistics but lie in a proper span. Gaussian elimination is the disclosed Track-B reference algorithm, while the intended route is to notice the single orbit under the displayed coordinate cycle.
