I’ve selected the parity-set-system version as the coherent result: it is a genuine Test Cover instance (items and tests are still the objects being verified), and it has a cleaner Track B gap—incremental exact Gaussian elimination versus recognizing one cyclic orbit. Before accepting it, I found and am correcting four audit issues in that concurrent draft: the profile’s domain/regime, a hard-coded G5 pass, missing monotonicity in G7, and an undercounted compact-route cost. I’m also keeping every potential shipping rung under the 300-operation cap.
