Implemented a self-contained Track B parity Test Cover generator based on the paper’s native set-system problem. The [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.17948) was checked against its full text, including Theorems 1–3 and Sections 3–5.

Deliverables:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2411.17948/gen_2411_17948.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2411.17948/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2411.17948/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2411.17948/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2411.17948/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2411.17948/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- All G1–G8 and G9(c) checks pass.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Four attacks: 0/8 each.
- Gaussian reference: 8/8, averaging 15,097 operations.
- Compact orbit route: 141 measured operations, 267 worst-case bound.
- Answer: 76 characters and 19 elements.
- An additional 100 shipping seeds passed construction, Gaussian recovery, and compact recovery.

The required oracle audit remains blocked. OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)` for every bare, hinted, and placebo call, so all arms correctly record 0 valid attempts. The family has not been rejected, but it must not be considered hardened until rerun with a funded `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`:

```bash
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_2411_17948.py
```
